<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103980" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίμ-ησις</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῑ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>holding valuable,
				honouring, esteeming</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				696d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				728e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>estimation</i> or <i>valuation</i> of property or
			merchandise, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PRev.Laws</u>
				29.12
			</span></i>, al. <span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				12.1
			</span></i>, al. <span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				31.28.3
			</span></i>: pl., <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				364.66
			</span></i> (Ephesus, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς
				τ. προσεξεπλήρωσεν</span>, = Lat. <i>census
				explevit,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Mon.Anc.Gr.
				19.10
			</span></i>: 
				Dor.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίμᾱσις</span></b> , 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρπῶ</span>”
				<i>Docum.ant.dell' Africa Italiana</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.88
				</span></i>
			 (Cyrene, <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>assessment of damages</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				878e
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ποιεῖν τινι</span> (opp. a
			capital charge) <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				5.10
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαντᾶν εἰς τὴν τ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.198
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				53.18
			</span></i>: 
				Dor.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίμᾱσις</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Foed.Delph.Pell.</u>
				1
			</span></i>A <i><span class="en">
				9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>rating</i> or <i>assessment</i> for political purposes, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1308b2
			</span></i> (pl.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ τιμήσεως πολίτευμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					18.18
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς πολίτας συντάξαι . . κατὰ τιμήσεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plot.
					6.3.1
				</span></i>
			; of the Roman <i>census</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				1.74
			</span></i>: pl., <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				3.5.3
			</span></i>: pl. of one <i>census</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				55
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>payment</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				4.327.10
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>.</div>
